(1274, 4650, '_cmb_description_text', '<table>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"80%\">\r\n      <h3><strong>Chief Executive Officer</strong></h3>\r\n      <strong>Engr. Muhammad Zafar</strong>\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em>M.Sc. (Electrical)</em>\r\n      <em>University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Lahore</em>\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em\r\n        >B.Sc. (Electrical) Mehran University of Engineering and Technology\r\n        (MUET), Jamshoro</em\r\n      >\r\n      <br />\r\n      He served NTDC for over 36 years and retired as General Manager. In 1982\r\n      he joined WAPDA as Assistant Director (Inspection). He executed his\r\n      obligations for almost 12 years as SDO (GSC) South, (WAPDA) Hyderabad. He\r\n      served for 4 years as Executive Engineer (EHV) Construction Division\r\n      Lahore and for 1 year in S &amp; I as well. For two (02) years of\r\n      deputation at NPCC (Saudia Arabia) as Senior Engineer, performed his\r\n      obligation against construction of 380kV Transmission Line from Makkah to\r\n      Taif and 380kV In &amp; Out arrangement at Khulais Substation. Six years’\r\n      experience as Executive Engineer GC Division Lahore for construction of\r\n      66kV to 132kV Transmission Line and Grid Station Projects in Lahore\r\n      region. Three years of experience as Project Director EHV-II NTDC Multan\r\n      for management and construction of 220kV to 500kV Transmission Line and\r\n      Grid Station Projects in Multan and Southern region. Three years’\r\n      experience as Chief Engineer EHV-II NTDC Hyderabad for management and\r\n      construction of 220kV to 500kV Transmission Line and Grid Station Projects\r\n      across the country.\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"20%\">\r\n      <a\r\n        href=\"https://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/picture-e1580440918913.jpg\"\r\n        ><img\r\n          class=\"alignnone wp-image-4654\"\r\n          src=\"https://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/picture-e1580440918913-296x300.jpg\"\r\n          alt=\"Engr. Muhammad Zafar, Chief Executive Officer\"\r\n          width=\"191\"\r\n          height=\"194\"\r\n      /></a>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"80%\">\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n      <h3><strong>General Manager (Power)</strong></h3>\r\n      <strong>Engr. Muhammad Saleem</strong>\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em\r\n        >M.Sc. (Electrical, University of Engineering and Technology (UET),\r\n        Lahore</em\r\n      >\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em>MBA University of the Punjab</em>\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em\r\n        >B.Sc. (Electrical) Honors, University of Engineering and Technology\r\n        (UET), Lahore</em\r\n      >\r\n      <br />\r\n      <p>\r\n        He served WAPDA/LESCO/PEPCO for 39 years and retired as General\r\n        Manager.  He remained posted as Chief Executive Officer LESCO and\r\n        General Manager PEPCO. He joined WAPDA in 1979 as Sub Divisional\r\n        Officer. He remained posted as SDO Construction, Street Light, and\r\n        various Sub Divisions of Operation.  He served as Executive Engineer\r\n        Operation, M&amp;T, Deputy Director Planning, Commercial, M&amp;O,\r\n        Inventory Control &amp; Commercial Surveillance.  As Superintending\r\n        Engineer, he served as SE GSO, &amp; SE Operation.  He Served as Chief\r\n        Engineer T&amp;G &amp; Technical Director LESCO.  He has vast experience\r\n        of Distribution, Operation, Construction, Grid Stations and Transmission\r\n        Lines maintenance.\r\n      </p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"20%\">\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n   <br />\r\n      <a\r\n        href=\"https://www.barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Muhammad-Saleem.jpg\"\r\n        ><img\r\n          class=\"alignnone wp-image-4721\"\r\n          src=\"https://www.barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Muhammad-Saleem-270x300.jpg\"\r\n          alt=\"Engr. Muhammad Saleem, General Manager (Power)\"\r\n          width=\"174\"\r\n          height=\"194\"\r\n      /></a>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"80%\">\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n      <h3><strong>GM (Water &amp; Coordination)</strong></h3>\r\n      <strong>Engr. Abdul Samad Qureshi</strong>\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em\r\n        >M.Sc. (Irrigation/Hydraulics) Asian Institute of Technology (AIT),\r\n        Bangkok, Thailand</em\r\n      >\r\n      <br />\r\n      <em\r\n        >B.Sc. (Civil) University of Engineering and Technology (UET),\r\n        Lahore</em\r\n      >\r\n      <p>\r\n        Practicing professional Engineer since 1970 has served in LDA water wing\r\n        Lahore and Kano State Urban Development Board, Nigeria, Consultant to\r\n        WAPDA on Dasu Dam Hydropower Project and Project Manager with BARQAAB\r\n        Consulting Services on Third Party Monitoring Project of Irrigation\r\n        Department Punjab. As Founder Member of Nespak, as Vice President,\r\n        Construction Management Division. He has been working at the top\r\n        management positions both as Supervisory Consultant and as\r\n        <em>the Engineer </em>of the Projects, dealing with the Funding Agencies\r\n        namely, World Bank (IDA}, Asian Development Bank, USAID, JBIC (JICA) and\r\n        KfW (FIDIC). Work experience is both in Pakistan and Overseas (Nigeria,\r\n        Azerbaijan and Thailand).\r\n      </p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"20%\">\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n      <br />\r\n      <a\r\n        href=\"https://www.barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Abdul-Samad-Qureshi.jpg\"\r\n        ><img\r\n          class=\"alignnone wp-image-4725\"\r\n          src=\"https://www.barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Abdul-Samad-Qureshi-254x300.jpg\"\r\n          alt=\"Engr. Abdul Samad Qureshi, General Manager (W&C)\"\r\n          width=\"175\"\r\n          height=\"206\"\r\n      /></a>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n'),
