(4389, 1, '2014-11-21 07:09:55', '2014-11-21 07:09:55', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">CHASHMA <BR> RIGHT BANK CANAL <BR><span class=\"accent\"> (LIFT CUM GRAVITY) PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n<h2>DETAILED DESIGN AND TENDER DOCUMENTS</BR>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_full]\r\n\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided technical services in the Project for Planning, Detailed Hydraulic and Structural Design, Environmental Impact Assessment, Resettlement Action Plan, Geological Investigations, Model Studies Supervision. </p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Project of CRBC (Lift cum Gravity) canal envisages irrigation of over 286,000 acres of land in D. I. Khan District, contiguous with right bank of existing CRBC Gravity System, through a lift cum gravity canal off-taking from Indus river at Chashma Barrage.  Project comprises a new intake structure with design discharge of 2,613 cusecs a feeder canal of about 39-km length.  Main Canal of about 73-km length 25 Nos. Distributaries of 167-km length and 24 No. Minors of 102 canal miles length on farm developments of proposed command area through watercourses and flood protection and drainage works are also proposed.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 158,45 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 100%.\r\nDate of Commencement: June 2002.\r\nDate of Completion: January 2004.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'CHASHMA RIGHT BANK CANAL', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'chashma-right-bank-canal', '', '', '2014-11-21 07:18:55', '2014-11-21 07:18:55', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4389', 36, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4391, 1, '2014-11-21 07:22:27', '2014-11-21 07:22:27', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">GREATER THAL CANAL<span class=\"accent\"> PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n<h2>DETAILED ENGINEERING STUDIES, TENDER DOCUMENTS AND CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISION</BR>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_full]\r\n\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided technical expert services in the Project for Detailed Design of Canal, preparation of Detailed Design for Canal Command Network of distributaries & minors, design of drainage measures to minimize waterlogging and salinity problems arising from project implementation.  The Consultants would also design the E & M works on the canal and conduct Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) and prepare Resettlement Action Plan (RAP).  The Consultants shall prepare Tender Drawings and documents for construction and carry out Construction of works.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Greater Thal Canal Project (GTCP) is one of the priority projects under WAPDA’s Water Vision 2025 Program. It falls in the territory of Jhang, Khushab, Bhakkar and Layyah districts.  The Project comprises an irrigation system network transmitting 8,500 cusecs discharge to irrigate an area of about 1,918,000 acres of Thal Doab (the area between Indus and Jhelum rivers).  The Irrigation System consists of main Canal 22.5 miles, branch and sub-branch canal 223 miles and distributaries / minors 1,221 miles along with other allied structure, regular, falls, bridges etc.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 158,45 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 100%.\r\nDate of Commencement: March 2002.\r\nDate of Completion: December 2008.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'GREATER THAL CANAL PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'greater-thal-canal-project', '', '', '2014-11-21 07:32:36', '2014-11-21 07:32:36', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4391', 37, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4390, 1, '2014-11-21 07:11:09', '2014-11-21 07:11:09', '[column_full]\n<h1 class=\"giga\">CHASHMA <RIGHT BANK CANAL</h1>\n<h2 class=\"accent\">(LIFT CUM GRAVITY) PROJECT</h2>\n<BR><h2>ETAILED DESIGN AND TENDER DOCUMENTS</BR>\n[/column_full]\n[column_full]\n<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-3983\" src=\"https://barqaab.com.-content/uploads/2014/11/kachi-canal.jpg\" alt=\"Rainee Canal\" width=\"1100\" />\n[/column_full]\n[column_two_thirds]\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided technical services in the Project for Planning, Detailed Hydraulic and Structural Design, Environmental Impact Assessment, Resettlement Action Plan, Geological Investigations, Model Studies Supervision. </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Project of CRBC (Lift cum Gravity) canal envisages irrigation of over 286,000 acres of land in D. I. Khan District, contiguous with right bank of existing CRBC Gravity System, through a lift cum gravity canal off-taking from Indus river at Chashma Barrage.  Project comprises a new intake structure with design discharge of 2,613 cusecs a feeder canal of about 39-km length.  Main Canal of about 73-km length 25 Nos. Distributaries of 167-km length and 24 No. Minors of 102 canal miles length on farm developments of proposed command area through watercourses and flood protection and drainage works are also proposed.</p>\n[/column_two_thirds]\n[column_third]\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 158,45 Million.\nBARQAAB Share: 100%.\nDate of Commencement: June 2002.\nDate of Completion: January 2004.</p>\n[/column_third]', 'CHASHMA RIGHT BANK CANAL', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '4389-autosave-v1', '', '', '2014-11-21 07:11:09', '2014-11-21 07:11:09', '', 4389, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/2014/11/4389-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(4392, 1, '2014-11-21 07:32:26', '2014-11-21 07:32:26', '', 'greaterthalcanal', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'greaterthalcanal', '', '', '2014-11-21 07:32:26', '2014-11-21 07:32:26', '', 4391, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/greaterthalcanal.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4393, 1, '2014-11-21 08:13:00', '2014-11-21 08:13:00', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">CONSTRUCTION OF SPILLWAY<span class=\"accent\"> <BR>LINED CHANNEL AND APPURTENANT STRUCTURE ON SPILLWAY PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n<h2>RASUL HYDEL POWER STATION</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_full]\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-3983\" src=\"https://barqaab.com.-content/uploads/2014/11/canal5.jpg\"/>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided technical expert services in the Project for preparation of tender documents, estimates and contract evaluation.  Construction Supervision of Syphonic Spillway, Lined Channel and related structures including falls, outfall structure and trash cleaning arrangements.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The proposed Spillway Project at Rasul Hydel Power Station lies on the Right Bank of Rasul Power Channel (RPC) adjacent to Rasul Power Station.  It is about 11 KM north-east of Mandi Bahauddin and forms the central portion of the Chaj Doab lying between the Jhelum and Chenab rivers.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The proposed Spillway Project at Rasul Hydel Power Station lies on the Right Bank of Rasul Power Channel (RPC) adjacent to Rasul Power Station.  It is about 11 KM north-east of Mandi Bahauddin and forms the central portion of the Chaj Doab lying between the Jhelum and Chenab rivers.</p>\r\n\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 93 Million.\r\nDate of Commencement: January 2003.\r\nDate of Completion: January 2005.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'RASUL HYDEL POWER STATION', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'rasul-hydel-power-station', '', '', '2014-11-21 08:14:21', '2014-11-21 08:14:21', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4393', 38, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4394, 1, '2014-11-21 08:10:45', '2014-11-21 08:10:45', '', 'rasulhydel', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'canal5', '', '', '2014-11-21 08:10:54', '2014-11-21 08:10:54', '', 4393, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/canal5.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4395, 1, '2014-11-21 08:17:56', '2014-11-21 08:17:56', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">RIGHT BANK <span class=\"accent\"><BR>OUTFALL DRAIN <BR>(RBOD-III) </span></h1>\r\n<h2>DETAILED DESIGN, FEASIBILITY STUDIES AND CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISION</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided Consultancy Services as a Joint Venture for Feasibility Studies, Detailed Design, Tender Documents and Construction Supervision of RBOD-III in Sindh Province.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Services consist of carrying out feasibility studies of Shahdad Kot Unit, preparation of Detailed Design, Tender Documents, Tender Evaluation and Construction Supervision of drainage works. </p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Project is located in Sindh and comprises feasibility studies, Detailed Engineering Design and Construction Supervision of Shahdad Kot unit drainage disposal of Balochistan, MNV Drain, Carrier Drain and other drains of Indus Right Bank to ultimately outfall into the Indus Link and Indus River.</p>\r\n\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 114.96 Million.\r\nDate of Commencement: July 2004.\r\nDate of Completion: June 2009.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'RIGHT BANK OUTFALL DRAIN RBOD III ', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'right-bank-outfall-drain-rbod-iii', '', '', '2014-11-21 08:18:42', '2014-11-21 08:18:42', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4395', 39, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4396, 1, '2014-11-21 08:21:02', '2014-11-21 08:21:02', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">SUKKER BARRAGE<span class=\"accent\"><BR> REHABILITATION AND IMPROVEMENT PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n<h2>DESIGN & SUPERVISION</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB has undertaken this project on Sukkur Barrage on river Indus. BARQAAB is carrying out Design Construction Supervision this Project in association with ACE. The Project includes rehabilitation of Sukkur Barrage Design and Construction Supervision of works associated in its improvement and proper functioning.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">\r\nDate of Commencement: March 2010.\r\nDate of Completion: March 2013.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'SUKKER BARRAGE REHABILITATION AND IMPROVEMENT PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'sukker-barrage-rehabilitation-and-improvement-project', '', '', '2014-11-21 08:21:02', '2014-11-21 08:21:02', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4396', 40, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4397, 1, '2014-11-21 08:24:13', '2014-11-21 08:24:13', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">LINING OF ROHRI CANAL<span class=\"accent\"> <BR>DADU CANAL <BR>AND RICE CANAL</span></h1>\r\n<h2>FEASIBILITY STUDY, DETAILED ENGINEERING DESIGN, TENDER DOCUMENTS AND PC-I</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQABB provided services for Feasibility Study, Detailed Engineering Design, Tender Documents and PC-I of Rohri, Dadu and Rice Canals with a Joint Venture with ACE.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Carry out Condition Survey of all the three canals, establish their existing status of herms and prism, inventory of structures, settlements around the canal alignment, Geo-Tech investigations. The project studies included Lining methods under canal flow conditions, selection of Lining options and preparation of cost estimates, environmental and Socio-economic studies etc and process a general consensus to develop Pilot project for Technically feasible and economically viable Lining options.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided Services in Hydraulics and Structural Design Economic and Socio-Economic studies, Surveys through GIS, Costing and other design related fields.</p>\r\n\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 85 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 25%.\r\nDate of Commencement: July 2009.\r\nDate of Completion: March 2010.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'LINING OF ROHRI CANAL, DADU CANAL AND RICE CANAL', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'lining-of-rohri-canal-dadu-canal-and-rice-canal', '', '', '2014-11-21 08:24:52', '2014-11-21 08:24:52', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4397', 41, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4398, 1, '2014-11-21 08:28:44', '2014-11-21 08:28:44', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">INSTITUTIONAL STRENGTHENING,<span class=\"accent\"> <BR>CAPACITY BUILDING AND<BR>IMPROVED OPERATION MANAGEMENT</span></h1>\r\n<h2>OF THE CANAL SYSTEM OF LBDCIP-PACKAGE-5</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Study both the existing irrigation operation and irrigation management in the Project Area and those in LCC command where management transfer has commenced. Review of procedures for information of KPs’ and FOs, highlight deficiencies and suggest improvements. Review of strategies/polices initiated by PIDA for participation of water user in irrigation management laws/rules framed by PIDA for opreationalization of FO’s, their effectiveness and highlight weaknesses along with suggestion for improvement. Carry out awareness raising, educating rights, and Management skills development.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\"Strengthening and Capacity Building  of Farmers Organization (FO) and Area Water Boards (AWB), Provide Training, Training of Trainers, Management Development, Abiana Assessment , Financial Management, Irrigation Management.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided services for this ADB funded Project as a joint venture partner of 25% share. The project aims at Institutional reforms, formation of AWBs and FOs and then effective working Capacity Building and training.</p>\r\n\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: 14,700 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 25%.\r\nDate of Commencement: February 2010.\r\nDate of Completion: January 2014.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'CANAL SYSTEM OF LBDCIP-PACKAGE-5', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'canal-system-of-lbdcip-package-5', '', '', '2014-11-21 08:29:22', '2014-11-21 08:29:22', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4398', 42, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4384, 1, '2014-11-20 09:26:37', '2014-11-20 09:26:37', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">RAINEE CANAL PROJECT</h1>\r\n<h2 class=\"accent\">DETAILED ENGINEERING DESIGN, TENDER DOCUMENTATION AND CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISION</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_full]\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-3983\" src=\"https://barqaab.com.-content/uploads/2014/11/rainee.jpg\" alt=\"Rainee Canal\" width=\"1100\" />\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_full]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB is independently providing the above Consultancy Services for Rainee Canal Project of discharge of 10,000 cusecs. It involves Guddu Barrage Works of extension of Left Divide Wall, River Training Works with one J-Spur on right bank of the river upstream and Canal Head Regulator etc. Main Canal, Branch Canals and Distributaries have number of Structures. Model Studies were also conducted for the major structures.</p>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The services included preparation of detailed design, Engineer’s estimate, Tender Documents, Evaluation of Tenders and Construction Supervision of Rainee Canal. The work also involves assistance in model studies of head regulators and geotechnical investigations of structures. Work comprises of Construction of 10,000 cusecs Head Regulator, Silt Excluder and Skimming Platform on Indus river for Rainee Canal, Construction of Spur on Indus river at Guddu Barrage and Construction of 5 Nos. Cross-Regulators and Complex Structures.</p>\r\n&nbsp;\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The services included preparation of detailed design, Engineer’s estimate, Tender Documents, Evaluation of Tenders and Construction Supervision of Rainee Canal. The work also involves assistance in model studies of head regulators and geotechnical investigations of structures. Work comprises of Construction of 10,000 cusecs Head Regulator, Silt Excluder and Skimming Platform on Indus river for Rainee Canal, Construction of Spur on Indus river at Guddu Barrage and Construction of 5 Nos. Cross-Regulators and Complex Structures.</p>\r\n[/column_full]', 'RAINEE CANAL PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'rainee-canal-project', '', '', '2014-11-20 09:36:05', '2014-11-20 09:36:05', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4384', 34, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4385, 1, '2014-11-20 09:23:42', '2014-11-20 09:23:42', '', 'rainee', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'rainee', '', '', '2014-11-20 09:23:42', '2014-11-20 09:23:42', '', 4384, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/rainee.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4387, 1, '2014-11-20 11:17:35', '2014-11-20 11:17:35', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">KACHHI CANAL PROJECT</h1>\r\n<h2 class=\"accent\">DETAILED ENGINEERING DESIGN, TENDER DOCUMENTS AND PERFORMANCE EVALUATION OF HILL TORRENT MANAGEMENT AND CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISION</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_full]\r\n<img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-3983\" src=\"https://barqaab.com.-content/uploads/2014/11/kachi-canal.jpg\" alt=\"Rainee Canal\" width=\"1100\" />\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">BARQAAB provided technical expert services in the Project for review of Model Studies, preparation of RAP and sociological studies, Detailed Engineering Design, Cost Estimation and Preparation of Tender Documents. And Construction Supervision. In addition the Consultant will carryout the drainage studies and Design and submit a hill torrent management plan. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Balochistan is the largest province of the country.  Large tracts of fertile and fairly levelled land are available for cultivation in Kachhi Plain.  The Kachhi Canal Project envisaged, irrigation of over 713,000 acres of land.  The off-take of the canal from Taunsa Barrage at Indus in Punjab province. The total length of main canal is 500-km in which 300-km in Punjab and 200-km used channel in Balochistan province.  Length of the distributaries and minors is 2000-km and the discharge capacity of the canal is 7,000 cusecs. 64 No. Cross-drainage structure, 83 No. V.R. Bridge and 5 No. A.R. Bridges are proposed to be constructed.  The consortium comprises carrying out Detailed Design, preparation of Tender Document, tender evaluation and Construction Supervision of all works. In addition the Consultant will carryout the drainage studies and Design and submit a hill torrent management plan. </p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 31,204 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 100%.\r\nDate of Commencement: December 2003.\r\nDate of Completion: June 2010.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'KACHHI CANAL PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'kachhi-canal-project', '', '', '2014-11-20 11:19:31', '2014-11-20 11:19:31', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4387', 35, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4383, 1, '2014-11-20 09:13:18', '2014-11-20 09:13:18', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">PREPARATION OF<span class=\"accent\"> FEASIBILITY STUDY FOR NAI GAJ DAM PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_full]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Project envisages construction of a 59 m high dam and appurtenant works on Nai Gaj river in a period of 48 months. The gross storage capacity of the dam would be 0.370 BCM (0.30 MAF) with a life of 40 years. A spillway to cater for a probable maximum flood of 21,103 cumecs (745,360 cusecs) is also part of the design. The Project is designed to irrigate 16,187.45 hectare (40,000 acres) of culturable command area (CCA) either through surface, sprinkler, drip or mixed irrigation system and produce 17 GWh energy from the irrigation releases. The total cost of the dam, appurtenant structures and irrigation system would be Rs. 17,797 million while the cost of development of the command area through surface, sprinkler, drip and mixed irrigation systems would be Rs. 10.80 million, Rs. 2,592 million, Rs. 2,160 million and Rs. 1,728 million respectively. Hence the total base cost of the Project with surface, sprinkler, drip and mixed irrigation systems would be Rs. 17,807.80 million, Rs. 20,389 million, Rs. 19, 957 million and Rs. 19,525 million, respectively.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The combined storage of these reservoirs totals 3.15 MAF, which would irrigate 353,000 acres of land under conventional flood irrigation means while the area under irrigation would rise to approximately 600,000 acres once micro irrigation methods of sprinkler and drip are introduced.</p>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_third]\r\n', 'FEASIBILITY STUDY FOR NAI GAJ DAM PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'feasibility-study-for-nai-gaj-dam-project', '', '', '2014-11-20 09:14:01', '2014-11-20 09:14:01', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4383', 27, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4381, 1, '2014-11-20 09:05:23', '2014-11-20 09:05:23', '', '33827065', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '33827065', '', '', '2014-11-20 09:05:23', '2014-11-20 09:05:23', '', 4380, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/33827065.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4382, 1, '2014-11-20 09:08:19', '2014-11-20 09:08:19', '[column_full]\n<h1 class=\"giga\">MIRANI DAM <span class=\"accent\"> PROJECT</span></h1>\n[/column_full]\n\n[column_two_thirds]\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Contract Documents of Preparatory Works in Mirani Dam Project.</h2>\n<BR><h2>The project was completed by Barqaab independently without association.</h2>\n[/column_two_thirds]\n[column_third]\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Dam Type: Earth Fill.\nHeight: 127 feet..\nGross Storage: 0.302 MAF.\nLive Storage: 0.152 MAF.\nDead Storage: 0.150 MAF.\nCultureable Command Area: 33,200 Acres\n</p>\n[/column_third]', 'MIRANI DAM PROJECT', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '4380-autosave-v1', '', '', '2014-11-20 09:08:19', '2014-11-20 09:08:19', '', 4380, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/2014/11/4380-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(4370, 1, '2014-11-20 08:33:42', '2014-11-20 08:33:42', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">20MW PUNJNAD <BR>LOW HEAD <BR> <span class=\"accent\"> HYDROPOWER PROJECT</span></h1><h2>( Feasibilty Study)</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Consultancy Services Include supervision of survey and investigation work conducted on the program prepared by Consultants and Carrying out Feasibility Study of the hydropower project and prepare an acceptable and bankable report of the project covering Feasibility level Design and drawings of each structure, Bill of Quantities, Cost estimates, Powerhouse and Power plant, hydro mechanical, electrical and miscellaneous auxiliary equipment (Technical particulars, numbers, capacity etc.), Economic & Financial Analysis, Environmental Impact Assessment, Workout cost per KWh of power production, Prepare and provide the Hydrological, Geotechnical and Topographical Survey Report, Alternative Layouts and Comparison, IEE Social and Resettlement Report and Feasibility Report.</p>\r\n\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The main objective of Punjnad Low Head Hydropower Project is to utilize the flows of River Chenab at Punjnad Barrage to generate 18 MW power and supply into national grid system immediately. The project, falling in the load centre area will be connected to the nearest grid station and thus will contribute to the national grid with minimum line losses and no substantial cost for transmission line.</p>\r\n\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Proposed Punjnad Low Head Hydropower Project will be constructed along the right bank of Punjnad Barrage on Chenab River. The project area is located on the right bank of Punjnad Barrage. The headrace and the powerhouse are at a distance of 608 m away from the centerline of the Barrage. The powerhouse is estimated to have an installed capacity of 18 MW and an annual energy output of 58 GWh at 30% probability time with available head ranging between 2.0 to 5.0 m. The powerhouse including service bay has a length of 75.95 m and width of 49.18 m.  The total length including upstream and downstream concrete floors is 65.97 m. The designed foundation level is fixed at EL 86.22 whereas the top elevation of the powerhouse is at 115.00 m. The headrace comprises trapezoidal cross-section having total length of approximately 840 m and a bed width of 80 m.  The top width is approximately 111.52 m and the average depth is about 4.46 m. The tailrace comprising trapezoidal cross-section has a length of approximately 230 m and a bed width of 96 m.  The top width is 132.04 m.</p>\r\n\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">\r\nDate of Commencement: April 2008\r\nDate of Completion: November 2008\r\n[/column_third]', '20 MW PUNJNAD LOW HEAD HYDROPOWER PROJECT', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', '4367-autosave-v1', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:33:42', '2014-11-20 08:33:42', '', 4367, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/2014/11/4367-autosave-v1/', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(4371, 1, '2014-11-20 08:36:46', '2014-11-20 08:36:46', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">GARUK DAM<span class=\"accent\"> PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Updated Design / Main Report Design, Drawings, Specifications & Updated Pc-I Performa.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Consultants reviewed and update the feasibility study of Pelar Storage Dam Project. Updating of the feasibility study involves hydrological studies (water availability, sediment and flood studies), design aspects (structural, hydraulic, geotechnical and hydro-mechanical), hydropower potential, soil survey, agricultural study (cropping pattern, crop water requirements, yields and returns) EIA study, cost estimates (civil, electrical, mechanical works environmental mitigation, project engineering , management and contingencies), economic analysis, financial analysis and preparation of updated feasibility report.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A potential storage site is available on Garuk River in District Kharan of Balochistan Province for the construction of a dam. An Embankment Dam approximately 55 meter (180.5 ft) high across Garuk River will create a reservoir of about 50,695 AF gross capacity and 24,895 AF live storage. This will provide assured regulated supplies to the existing command area of about 12,500 acres downstream the Garuk River. From escape structure, regulated flow will be conveyed to a main pipe line having 60 cusecs capacity.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 4.6 Billion.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 100%.\r\nDate of Commencement: August 2009.\r\nDate of Completion: April 2010.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'GARUK DAM', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'garuk-dam', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:36:46', '2014-11-20 08:36:46', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4371', 21, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4372, 1, '2014-11-20 08:40:07', '2014-11-20 08:40:07', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">GOMAL ZAM DAM</h1><h2>DEVELOPMENT OF DESIGN CONCEPTS AFTER INVESTIGATION</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Collection of data, review, formulation of programme for additional survey, evaluation of available and proposed geological mapping of dam and appurtenant structures, preliminary study of rock cut slopes, design of Adit on right abutment for investigation, preparation of tender documents and preparation of studies report on materials.  Development of Design Concepts for diversion during construction and shifting of power house in the body of the dam.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Gomal Zam Dam Multipurpose Project located in South Wazirastan, KPK on river Gomal is an RCC Dam with a Barrage at Kot Murtaza.  An irrigation system off-takes from this barrage to feed an area. Of 163,000 Acres in D.I.Khan plain.  The dam has a height of 436 feet and a live storage of 0.892 MAF and a generation capacity of 17.4 MW.  The dam is proposed to be construction on turnkey basis.</p>\r\n\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">\r\nDate of Commencement: May 2001.\r\nDate of Completion: August 2001.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'GOMAL ZAM DAM PROJECT ', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'gomal-zam-dam-project', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:41:41', '2014-11-20 08:41:41', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4372', 22, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4374, 1, '2014-11-20 08:46:45', '2014-11-20 08:46:45', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">SANJWAL – AKHORI <span class=\"accent\"> DAM COMPLEX PROJECT</span></h1><h2>( Appraisal Study)</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Feasibility / Appraisal Report of the Project to assess whether the Project is technically feasible, environmentally suitable and socially acceptable. The study was independently carried out by BARQAAB. Identification of local land potential for irrigated agriculture and check potential of future development with regard to Irrigation and Power potential. </p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Feasibility / Appraisal Report of the Project to assess whether the Project is technically feasible, environmentally suitable and socially acceptable. Identification of local land potential for irrigated agriculture and check potential of future development with regard to Irrigation and Power potential.  Carryout Environmental and Resettlement Studies and preparation of EIA.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Development of reservoir on Haro river and Nandana Kas with a 5 miles channel of 32000 cusecs to divert water from Tarbela reservoir a dam 240 ft. High would be constructed to develop irrigated agriculture in the region supplement the existing supplies from the Indus and Hydropower Generation. </p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">\r\nDate of Commencement: September 2001.\r\nDate of Completion: February 2002.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'SANJWAL – AKHORI DAM COMPLEX PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'sanjwal-akhori-dam-complex-project', '', '', '2014-11-21 09:27:03', '2014-11-21 09:27:03', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4374', 23, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4373, 1, '2014-11-20 08:39:46', '2014-11-20 08:39:46', '', 'gomal', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'gomal', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:39:46', '2014-11-20 08:39:46', '', 4372, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/gomal.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4376, 1, '2014-11-20 08:51:19', '2014-11-20 08:51:19', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">DHOK PATHAN <span class=\"accent\"> AND AKHORI DAM PROJECTS</span></h1><h2>( Appraisal Study)</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Feasibility / Appraisal Report of the Project to assess whether the Project is technically feasible, environmentally suitable and socially acceptable. Identification of local land potential for irrigated agriculture and check potential of future development.  Preparation of EIA and Resettlement Report with costing and suggestions of mitigation measures. </p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Development of reservoir (Akhori Dam) on Soan river and Nandana Kas with a 33 Km Channel of 82,000 cusec to divert water from Tarbela reservoir.  A dam of 418 ft. High at Nandana Kas and 190 ft. High at Soan river would be constructed to develop irrigation and supplement to the existing supplies from the Indus and provide Hydropower Generation.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 70 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 100%.\r\nDate of Commencement: July 2002.\r\nDate of Completion: October 2002.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'DHOK PATHAN DAM AND AKHORI DAM PROJECTS', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'dhok-pathan-dam-and-akhori-dam-projects', '', '', '2014-11-21 09:26:53', '2014-11-21 09:26:53', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4376', 24, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4375, 1, '2014-11-20 08:46:37', '2014-11-20 08:46:37', '', 'sanjwal', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'sanjwal', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:46:37', '2014-11-20 08:46:37', '', 4374, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/sanjwal.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4377, 1, '2014-11-20 08:51:04', '2014-11-20 08:51:04', '', 'dhok', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'dhok', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:51:04', '2014-11-20 08:51:04', '', 4376, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/dhok.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4378, 1, '2014-11-20 08:59:29', '2014-11-20 08:59:29', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">IMPLEMENTATION OF INDUS RIVER <span class=\"accent\"> TRIBUTARIES HIGH-HEAD HYDROPOWER COMPLEX</span></h1><h2>( DESIGN REVIEW AND CONSTRUCTION SUPERVISION OF HYDROPOWER PROJECT INCLUDING SWITCHYARD AND GRID STATIONS)</h2>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Consultancy Services include Contractors design review and construction supervision of three High Head Hydropower Projects. The project activities also include design of 2 Nos. bridges over Indus River near Besham in district Hazara, for access to powerhouse site as well as reservoir area. The span of the two bridges is 100 meter and 120 meter respectively. In addition preparation of cost of various components of the project and preparation of PC-1 proforma is to be done.</p>\r\n<BR><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The Project comprises utilising the discharge of tributaries of Indus river near Basham in KPK for Hydropower development namely Khan Khwar, Duber Khwar and Allai Khwar Hydropower Project with installed capacity of 72 MW, 130 MW and 121 MW respectively. Cost of the Project is Khan Khwar Rs. 8,301 million, Duber Khwar Rs. 16,324 million and Allai Khwar Rs. 8,577 million.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Total Project Cost: PKR 33,202 Million.\r\nBARQAAB Share: 22%.\r\nDate of Commencement: November 2002.\r\nDate of Completion: October 2010.</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'IMPLEMENTATION OF INDUS RIVER TRIBUTARIES HIGH-HEAD HYDROPOWER COMPLEX', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'implementation-of-indus-river-tributaries-high-head-hydropower-complex', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:59:29', '2014-11-20 08:59:29', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4378', 25, 'portfolios', '', 0),
(4379, 1, '2014-11-20 08:59:19', '2014-11-20 08:59:19', '', 'indusriver', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'open', '', 'indusriver', '', '', '2014-11-20 08:59:19', '2014-11-20 08:59:19', '', 4378, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/indusriver.jpg', 0, 'attachment', 'image/jpeg', 0),
(4380, 1, '2014-11-20 09:04:23', '2014-11-20 09:04:23', '[column_full]\r\n<h1 class=\"giga\">MIRANI DAM <span class=\"accent\"> PROJECT</span></h1>\r\n[/column_full]\r\n\r\n[column_two_thirds]\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Contract Documents of Preparatory Works in Mirani Dam Project.\r\n<BR>The project was completed by Barqaab independently without association.</p>\r\n[/column_two_thirds]\r\n[column_third]\r\n<p style=\"padding:50px 0px 50px 0px; border-style: dashed; border-width: 1px; font-weight:bold;\">Dam Type: Earth Fill.\r\nHeight: 127 feet..\r\nGross Storage: 0.302 MAF.\r\nLive Storage: 0.152 MAF.\r\nDead Storage: 0.150 MAF.\r\nCultureable Command Area: 33,200 Acres\r\n</p>\r\n[/column_third]', 'MIRANI DAM PROJECT', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'mirani-dam-project', '', '', '2014-11-20 09:08:36', '2014-11-20 09:08:36', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4380', 26, 'portfolios', '', 0);
