(4671, 3, '2020-01-31 04:20:01', '2020-01-31 04:20:01', '<h2 class=\"giga\">500kV GIRD STATIONS AND TRANSMISSIONS</h2>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>NTDC-KESC 500/220 kV INTERCONNECTION PROJECT (PHASE-I)</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Preparation of Bid Level Design, Bill of Quantities, Technical Specifications, Tender Document and Evaluation of the Bids.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost -</strong> PKR 284 Million and US$ 29.3 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share - </strong>100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement - </strong>June 2003\r\n<strong>Date of Completion - </strong>March 2004</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Two Nos. 500/220kV 3x200MVA Transformer Bay.\r\nTwo Nos. 220kV Line Bays.\r\nTwo Nos. 500kV Line Bays.\r\n5KM 500kV Transmission Line.\r\n15KM 220kV Transmission Line.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>NTDC-KESC 500/220 kV INTERCONNECTION PROJECT (PHASE-II)</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">500/220 kV GIS Grid station along with 500kV IN/OUT and 220kV Transmission Line Feeding KESC Network – Residency Construction Supervision Including Contract Administration, Quality Control, Contractors Claim Certification, Safety Programme, Follow Up and Revision Of Construction Schedules, Monitoring and Reporting Of Progress, Variation Orders and Design Changes During Execution, Testing And Commissioning, Final Completion Report And Handing Over The Project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost</strong> <strong>-</strong> PKR 284 Million and US$ 29.3 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share</strong> <strong>-</strong> 100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement</strong> <strong>-</strong> October 2004\r\n<strong>Date of Completion -</strong> December 2006</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Two Nos. 500/220kV 3x200MVA Transformer Bay.\r\nTwo Nos. 220kV Line Bays.\r\nTwo Nos. 500kV Line Bays.\r\n5KM 500kV Transmission Line.\r\n15KM 220kV Transmission Line.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500 kV MUZAFFARGARH AND GATTI TRANSMISSION LINE PROJECT</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Residency Construction Supervision Including Contract Administration, Quality Control, Contractors Claim Certification, Safety Programme, Follow Up and Revision of Construction Schedules, Monitoring and Reporting of Progress, Variation Orders and Design Changes During Execution Testing And Commissioning, Final Completion Report And Handing Over the Project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost</strong> <strong>-</strong> US$ 44 Million + PKR 458.9 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share - </strong>100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement</strong> <strong>-</strong> November 2005\r\n<strong>Date of Completion</strong> <strong>- </strong>September 2008</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">280km 500 kV Single Circuit, Quad Bundle Transmission Line from Muzzafargarh to Gatti.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500 kV MUZAFFARGARH AND GATTI GRID STATIONS EXTENSION PROJECT</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Residency Construction Supervision Including Contract Administration, Quality Control, Contractors Claim Certification, Safety Programme, Follow Up and Revision of Construction Schedules, Monitoring and Reporting of Progress, Variation Orders and Design Changes During Execution Testing And Commissioning, Final Completion Report And Handing Over the Project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost - </strong>US$ 36 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share - </strong>100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement</strong> <strong>-</strong> November 2005\r\n<strong>Date of Completion - </strong>December 2008</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong><em>Muzaffargarh Grid Station</em></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">One no. complete bay of breaker and half configuration for a 500kv line and an autotransformer.\r\n550/3kV, 3x37 MVAR Shut Reactor Bank with 1x37 MVAR spare unit.\r\nOne 525/220kV, 3x200MVA Autotransformer Bank with 1x200MVA spare unit.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong><em>Gatti Grid Station</em></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">One complete bay of breaker and half configuration for a 500kV line.\r\n550/3kV, 3x37MVAR Shunt Reactor Bank with 1x37 MVAR spare unit.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500kV GATTI GRID STATION EXTENSION PROJECT</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost</strong> <strong>-</strong> PKR 3500 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share</strong> <strong>-</strong> 100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement</strong> <strong>- </strong>August 2009\r\n<strong>Date of Completion</strong> <strong>-</strong> May 2010</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">2x600MVa, 500/220kV Auto-Transformer with Controlling Switchgear on both sides.\r\n2x250MVa, 220/132kV Auto-transformer with controlling switchgear on both sides.\r\n2x220kV Line Bay.\r\n1x6.3MVA, 132/11kV Power Transformer with controlling switchgear for auxiliary services.\r\n8x132kV Line Bays and one bus coupler bay.\r\nIn and Out of 500kV Guddu-Multan 2nd Circuit at DG Khan 500kV substation (20+20KM).</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500kV LAHORE (SHIEKHUPURA) GRID STATION PROJECT</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost</strong> <strong>- </strong>PKR 917 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share</strong> <strong>-</strong> 100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement</strong> <strong>-</strong> January 2008\r\n<strong>Date of Completion - </strong>February 2009</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">One No. 500/220kV, 3x200MVA Transformer Bay.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500/220kV DERA GHAZI KHAN SUBSTATION ALONG WITH ASSOCIATED 500KV AND 220KV TRANSMISSION LINES (PHASE-II)</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span class=\"style13\">Total Project Cost - </span><span class=\"style11\">PKR 3500 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share - </strong>100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement - </strong>February 2011\r\n<strong>Date of Completion - </strong>January 2013 </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">2x600MVa, 500/220kV Auto-Transformer with Controlling Switchgear on both sides.\r\n2x250MVa, 220/132kV Auto-transformer with controlling switchgear on both sides.\r\n2x220kV Line Bay.\r\n1x6.3MVA, 132/11kV Power Transformer with controlling switchgear for auxiliary services.\r\n8x132kV Line Bays and one bus coupler bay.\r\nIn and Out of 500kV Guddu-Multan 2nd Circuit at DG Khan 500kV substation (20+20KM).</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500/220kV GIS GHAZI BAROTHA GRID STATION EXTENSION PROJECT</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\">Preparation of Bid Level Design, Bill of quantities, Technical Specifications, Tender Document, Evaluation of the Bids, Residency Construction Supervision including Contract Administration, Quality Control, Contractors Claim Certification, Safety Programme, follow up and Revision of Construction Schedules, Monitoring and Reporting of Progress, Variation Orders and Design Changes during execution, Testing And Commissioning, Final Completion Report and Handing of Over The Project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Total Project Cost - </strong>PKR 1.654 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share - </strong>100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement - </strong>August 2009\r\n<strong>Date of Completion - </strong>June 2012</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">600MVA 500/220kV Auto Transformer Bay.\r\nAssociated Civil Works Foundations, Trenches, Walk way etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>500kV SHIKARPUR GRID STATION AND ASSOCIATED TRANSMISSION LINE PROJECT</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\">Preparation of Bid Level Design, Bill of quantities, Technical Specifications, Tender Document, Evaluation of the Bids, Residency Construction Supervision including Contract Administration, Quality Control, Contractors Claim Certification, Safety Programme, follow up and Revision of Construction Schedules, Monitoring and Reporting of Progress, Variation Orders and Design Changes during execution, Testing And Commissioning, Final Completion Report and Handing of Over The Project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\"><strong>Total Project Cost - </strong>PKR 8,050 Million\r\n<strong>Barqaab Share</strong> - 100%\r\n<strong>Date of Commencement</strong> <strong>-</strong> October 2010\r\n<strong>Date of Completion</strong> - September 2012</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\">2x600MVA, 500/220kV Transformers with allied equipment\r\n2x500kV S/C transmission Line 20+20 = 40KM on 3 bundle Greely Conductor for looping In/Out of 500kV Dadu-Guddu Circuit No.1 at Shikarpur new.\r\n2x500kV S/C Transmission Line 22+22=44KM on quad-Bundle Greely conductor for looping In/Out of 500kV Dadu-Guddu Circuit No.2 at Shikarpur.\r\n220kV D/C Transmission Line 50KM long on Single Rail Conductor for looping In/Out of 220kV Guddu-Sibbi S/C Shikarpur New.\r\nAssociated Civil Works Foundations, Trenches, Walk way etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"hr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"></div>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\"><strong>500kV TRANSMISSION SCHEME FOR DISPERSAL OF POWER FROM NEELUM-JHELUME HYDROPOWER PROJECT AS A JOINT VENTURE PARTNER WITH NESPAK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\" align=\"justify\">Preparation of Bid Level Design, Bill of quantities, Technical Specifications, Tender Document, Evaluation of the Bids, Residency Construction Supervision including Contract Administration, Quality Control, Contractors Claim Certification, Safety Programme, follow up and Revision of Construction Schedules, Monitoring and Reporting of Progress, Variation Orders and Design Changes during execution, Testing And Commissioning, Final Completion Report and Handing of Over The Project.  Working as Joint Venture Partner with NESPAK.</p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"style11\" style=\"text-align: left;\">235KM Long 500kV Single Circuit Transmission Line from Neelum-Jhelum to Gujranwala (Ghakkar).\r\n110KM Long 500kV single Circuit Quad Bundle Transmission Line from Neelum-Jhelum to Rewat.\r\nExtension by one Bay each in 500kV Substation at Rewat and Gujranwala (Ghakkar).</p>', '500kV GRID STATIONS AND TRANSMISSION LINES', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', '500kv-grid-stations-and-transmission-lines', '', '', '2020-01-31 12:27:23', '2020-01-31 12:27:23', '', 0, 'http://barqaab.com.pk/?post_type=portfolios&#038;p=4671', 0, 'portfolios', '', 0),
